# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]   (no dollar/backtick in the text)
register_gate "tests/test_billing_role.py" "BILLING ROLE GATE: PASS" "billing role" "billing role (the least-privilege WRITE seam reserved for future GitHub Marketplace entitlement handling: a dedicated veripsa_billing role whose ENTIRE reachable surface is USAGE on schema core plus EXECUTE on core.set_account_plan_with_authority(text,text,timestamptz) + its installation-keyed sibling -- the WRITE-side mirror of example_platform_reader, now ENFORCED as the COMPLEMENT. Connecting AS veripsa_billing it CAN set a plan and the abuse gate reflects it (the SAME footprint that walls a FREE account is lifted to NULL once paid), but is DENIED reading any core table [account/code_node/code_edge/event -- it cannot even read the plan it set, nor the moat], DENIED INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on any core table [it cannot set a plan by writing core.account directly, bypassing the gated normalizing setter], and DENIED any OTHER authority fn [transfer_repo_coordinate / set_plan_limit]; the buyer-self-upgrade perimeter stays intact [a buyer LOGIN role still cannot call the setter]; the App keeps its own EXECUTE on the setter -- veripsa_billing is added ALONGSIDE, not instead. PROD role-create + grant is PO-gated DDL.)" "billing role / LEAST-PRIVILEGE WRITE SEAM (future Marketplace billing can use a veripsa_billing connection that can ONLY call the plan setter -- not the App's full write surface, not any table, not any other authority fn; SECURITY-critical: it governs the quota wall and must not widen the write surface or the buyer perimeter)" "set_account_plan_with_authority is SECURITY DEFINER (runs as the migrator owner -- pins the account + arms the governed write internally), so a caller needs ONLY EXECUTE on it; veripsa_billing gets exactly that + USAGE on schema core and NOTHING else (no table grant, no other *_with_authority fn). The role is NOLOGIN in db/roles.sql (LOGIN+password out-of-band on prod, exactly like example_platform_reader); the grants live next to the App grant in db/schema/30_gate.sql (the App grant is unchanged). A future Marketplace entitlement worker can set CORE_BILLING_DB_URL with user=veripsa_billing and call core.set_account_plan_with_authority(p_gh_account_id, p_plan) only after entitlement sync and payer-org binding are implemented. This gate stands up the ephemeral Postgres + tightens the free line so the abuse wall bites on a small footprint, seeds a FREE account over the line (a real wall to lift) + a code_node moat row, ALTERs veripsa_billing LOGIN in its own ephemeral DB, then proves live: (1 ALLOW+ENFORCED) AS veripsa_billing it CAN SELECT set_account_plan_with_authority('123','pro') [returns ACCT-GH-123], core.account.plan becomes 'pro', and core._account_over_quota goes NULL [the same footprint that walled a FREE account is lifted]; (2 DENY-READ) SELECT on core.account/code_node/code_edge/event is permission-denied + has_table_privilege false, while the owner CAN read account [a real privilege difference]; (3 DENY-WRITE) INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on core.account is permission-denied + has_table_privilege false, and the denied direct UPDATE left plan='pro'; (4 DENY-AUTHORITY) transfer_repo_coordinate_with_authority + set_plan_limit_with_authority are permission-denied + has_function_privilege false; (5 PERIMETER) a buyer LOGIN role (veripsa_demo_agent3) is STILL denied the setter [no buyer self-upgrade] and changed nothing; plus CONTROL that veripsa_billing has EXACTLY one EXECUTE + schema USAGE [no CREATE], the owner has it too, and the App still has EXECUTE [its path untouched]; (6 COMPLEMENT -- audit iter-5 P3) the least-privilege claim ENFORCED against the live catalog: enumerate EVERY core fn and require veripsa_billing to have EXECUTE on EXACTLY the two plan setters and FALSE on EVERY OTHER one [the PUBLIC-EXECUTE default that used to leak ~40 read surfaces is stripped schema-wide in db/schema/99_least_privilege.sql; a new fn shipping PUBLIC-callable lands red here]. INERT until the PO applies the role-create + grant DDL on prod (PO-gated)." 30
